DOCUMENT();

loadMacros(
    "PGstandard.pl",    # Standard macros for PG language
    "PGML.pl",          # PGML markup and Math Objects
    "parserPopUp.pl",
    "PGcourse.pl",      # Customization file for the course
);

# Uncomment the following if you don't want to show which
# answers are correct and which are incorrect
#$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

$hlife = random(10,30,2);

@ans = ();

$ans[0] = sprintf("%0.1f",70/$hlife);


BEGIN_PGML
After introducing a disinfectent to a surface in a lab a population of bacteria has a half-life of around [$hlife] minutes. If this is the case, then the decay rate would be approximately [_]{$ans[0]}% per minute (rounded to the nearest tenth).

END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();
